WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:02.800
Recording. All right, here we go.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.920
Ladies and gentlemen, boys and girls and everyone along with

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.160
them. Welcome to Paragliding Atlas

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.600
2025. And today you're tuning in to a

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.360
very special note of thanks episode.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.840
And in case you're new here, I'm your host, Aninder Singh, and I

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.400
assure you that what's coming your way in the year 2025 will

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.640
be one of the most insightful, inspiring, and informative

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.280
content from the world of paragliding, brought to you by

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.080
the one and only Paragliding Atlas Podcast.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.160
But you know, before we dive deep into all of these exciting

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.080
bands, I was wondering what would be the best way to start

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.120
the journey for the new year ahead and for this show on a

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.800
positive note, or basically do something that promises to make

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.840
the world a better place from our end.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.040
And then I finally came up with a plan.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.720
But for this plan, I'd request you to take a moment with me and

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.160
make a pact. A promise to prioritise safety

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.720
and take care not only of ourselves, but for other pilots

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.480
sharing the airspace with us as well.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.920
You and I can ensure that we practice the highest levels of

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.720
flight safety every time we take to the skies in the sport of

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.000
paragliding. If you would allow me, I'd like

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.760
to share a story with you, a personal reflection on how I've

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.880
navigated my expectations and challenges in this space so far.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:35.800
And I kind of want to start with something as small as this

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.280
project right here. Because one thing that I've

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.120
learned over the past one year is that a lot of times, instead

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.200
of viewing any of the challenges as individual struggles, I just

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.600
try to see it through a lens of a larger community.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.000
And I can explain this with a more elaborate example because

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.560
let's say when I was looking to start an adventure within the

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.160
sport of paragliding, I was looking for something

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.880
meaningful, something impactful. You know, something that made

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.160
personal sense and commercial sense at the same time.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:09.320
Something that resonated with me deep inside and also good enough

00:02:09.919 --> 00:02:13.120
to put my heart and soul into it so that I can try and make a

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.040
living out of my passion. But of course there are multiple

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:19.840
challenges along chasing such a passion and I often kept on

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.040
running into obstacles, whether it was lack of ideas or

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.280
uncertainty about the next steps or feelings of self doubt,

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.880
anxiety, you name it, you have it kind of a thing.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.400
I mean everything would kind of creep in at some point in time

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.760
and again and make it harder to move forward.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.640
But then there was a paradigm shift when I basically decided

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.640
to zoom out. I started to think beyond just

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.440
myself. So instead of having the

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.400
question that what do I do to overcome these challenges which

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.880
were finding meaning and having it sustainable enough, I began

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.600
asking the question that what can I create that adds value to

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.160
the entire paraguiding community?

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.760
And I kid you not guys, this very simple shift was

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:05.440
transforming to say the least. And suddenly ideas just started

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.360
flowing in effortlessly. And the ease with which the

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.880
solution started appearing was, I mean to say, nothing short of

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.480
mesmerizing. You know, I, I can take you guys

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.960
back to the first episode that we recorded with Paul Tuckerts

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.960
about navigating Columbia. Because as a pilot myself, I

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:26.480
used to wonder and Google up endless sites, go to endless

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.120
Facebook posts and groups and look for information that, hey,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.240
I'm a wizarding pilot. What are the ways if I don't

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.480
want to hire a tour guide, you know, how do I figure out what

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.920
to do, what not to do, where to, you know, just the common

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.800
questions that come to your mind when you're visiting a new place

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.240
as a solo pilot. But then I was like, that is why

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.840
we need a show like this, which highlight how these airspaces

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.360
can be navigated with precaution and also be fun at the same

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.680
time. So that was the very first idea

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.160
of what happens to be the Paragliding Atlas podcast of

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.360
today. It all began with the desire to

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.640
create shared value and offer something meaningful, not just

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.320
for myself, but for all of you out there as well.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.640
And today, it's not only a moment of pride for me, but more

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.640
than that, it's a moment of immense gratitude.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.920
Because this show is the fastest growing show in the world of

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:26.920
paragliding all across interweb, having more than 5000 listeners

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.760
spanning across 70 countries and 30 industry experts sharing

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.560
their unfiltered wisdom and heartfelt knowledge with all of

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.760
us out there. And most importantly, none of

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.040
this would have been possible without your support.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.560
So thank you so much for being a part of this journey.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:51.040
And as we step into 2025, I'm beyond excited to share some

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.640
plans for the year ahead with you.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.280
And guess what? We're not just doubling down,

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.520
but we are tripling up the awesomeness that we make here

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.920
every week. So from a weekly release, we are

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.680
planning to go to a bi weekly episode release because this

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.120
allows us to cover a whole lot of topics.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.720
Because a lot of you guys have been reaching out and suggesting

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.080
endlessly interesting points of discussions.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.400
But having just one episode every week made it almost

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.160
impossible to cover all of those topics.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:28.280
So that's why we are bringing in a perfect mix of solo and guest

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.840
interviews all together. Bringing you a final product of

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:36.440
2 brand new episodes every week. Which means we're setting a

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.040
super ambitious target of 104 episodes this year.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.400
That's more than three times the content we have brought to you

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.800
so far. And today you happen to be

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.960
tuning in to a very first of these.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.560
But that's not all. Again, just like any other

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.080
challenge, there are so many questions.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.200
Will I be able to do it? What's going to happen, where

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.440
I'm going to find the topics, where I'm going to find the

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.080
guests, and how I'm going to keep the listeners engaged?

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.160
But here's the most exciting part, and this is where you come

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:11.280
in, because we plan to cover what is both endless and

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.960
enriching. So if you're stuck with me for

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:18.000
so far, this is where I'll explain you how your voice

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.480
matters. Because if there's a topic that

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.720
you've been curious about or a guest that you think could bring

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.480
immense value not just to the show, but to the entire

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.840
paragliding community, then I'd love to hear from you.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.440
So pick up your phone or get on your computer or reach out in

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:40.200
whichever way feels most convenient, whether it's e-mail,

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.120
Telegram, or WhatsApp. All of my contact information is

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.800
listed in the show notes below. And let's make this journey a

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.800
collaborative adventure where your ideas and feedback shape

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.920
the content that we create here at the Paragliding Atlas

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.040
Podcast. So as we embark on this

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.400
incredible journey in time to come, I'd like to leave you with

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.680
this. If you happen to have enjoyed

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:06.160
the show so far, don't keep it to yourself.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:10.400
Share it with your fellow pilots, your friends, or anyone

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.640
who loves the skies as much as we do.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.920
Because by spreading the word, we grow this community and most

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.120
importantly, make paragliding a safer and more enriching sport

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.840
for everyone. So on that note, I'm going to

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.520
leave you by saying what I always say.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:33.440
Stay tuned, stay excited, and remember the magic is just

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:34.160
getting started.
